Lab 11: Creating Virtual Machines in RHVM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Navigate and use the Red Hat Virtualization Manager (RHVM) web console effectively
Create and provision new virtual machines using RHVM interface
Configure essential VM resources including CPU, memory, storage, and network settings
Start virtual machines and verify their operational status
Understand the relationship between virtualization hosts and virtual machines
Apply best practices for VM resource allocation and management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of virtualization concepts and terminology
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Knowledge of basic networking concepts (IP addresses, subnets, VLANs)
Understanding of storage concepts (disk types, file systems)
Access to a web browser (Chrome, Firefox, or Edge recommended)
Basic knowledge of Red Hat Enterprise Linux operating system
Required Knowledge Areas
Virtualization Fundamentals: Understanding of hypervisors, virtual machines, and resource allocation
Linux Administration: Basic file system navigation and system administration concepts
Network Configuration: IP addressing, DNS, and basic network troubleshooting
Storage Management: Disk partitioning, file systems, and storage allocation concepts
