Troubleshooting Common Issues
VM Won't Start
Problem: VM fails to start or remains in "Powering Up" state

Solutions:

Check host resources:

Verify sufficient CPU and memory on target host
Review host status in Compute → Hosts
Verify storage connectivity:

Ensure storage domains are active
Check disk space availability
Review VM logs:

# On RHVM manager
tail -f /var/log/ovirt-engine/engine.log
Console Connection Issues
Problem: Cannot connect to VM console

Solutions:

Check browser settings:

Allow pop-ups for RHVM site
Install virt-viewer for SPICE console
Verify network connectivity:

Ensure firewall allows console ports
Check SPICE/VNC port configuration
Alternative console access:

Try different console type (SPICE vs VNC)
Use browser-based noVNC console
Performance Issues
Problem: VM running slowly or unresponsively

Solutions:

Check resource allocation:

Verify adequate CPU and memory allocation
Review host resource utilization
Optimize storage performance:

Use VirtIO drivers for better performance
Consider storage domain performance characteristics
Network optimization:

Use VirtIO network interfaces
Verify network configuration and bandwidth
Best Practices for VM Management
Resource Planning
CPU Allocation:

Don't over-allocate virtual CPUs
Consider CPU topology for application requirements
Monitor CPU ready time and utilization
Memory Management:

Set appropriate memory guarantees
Use memory ballooning for dynamic allocation
Monitor memory pressure and swapping
Storage Optimization:

Use thin provisioning for efficient space utilization
Implement appropriate disk interfaces (VirtIO-SCSI)
Plan for snapshot and backup storage requirements
Security Considerations
Network Security:

Implement appropriate network segmentation
Use VLANs for traffic isolation
Configure firewall rules as needed
Access Control:

Implement role-based access control
Use strong authentication mechanisms
Regular security updates and patches
